From e9c3f7cf3337429e5c0aa46c3f91dfd048ff3d6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lolren <loren.bufanu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 21:20:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] android: Enable the mainline software ISP Camera3 HAL

Make the generic Android HAL usable with minigbm buffers on the OnePlus 6T Waydroid armv7 image, add software NV12 output and keep software-ISP control latency bounded.

Translate exposure compensation, variable preview frame rates, autofocus modes/triggers/regions and result metadata between Camera2 and libcamera. Preserve valid sub-30-fps stream maps for sensors whose usable mode tops out at 15 fps, and report exposure, sensitivity and frame duration.

Use a bounded fast scan for explicit Android autofocus triggers while retaining local continuous refinement. This lets Camera2 clients open all three sensors, capture YUV/JPEG/private streams and use tap focus without vendor camera libraries.

Signed-off-by: Lolren <loren.bufanu@gmail.com>

